Plan D (future) = make the framework (ies-auto-mibs) an AgentX **subagent** instead of an in-process snmpd dlmod; before that, ies-auto-mibs will first be split into a shared library so everything can see it. Question verified 2026-07-01: **is any OID data trapped inside an individual daemon (which would force that daemon to also be a subagent)?** Answer: **No — two subagents (ISS + app_moxa_framework) suffice.**

Evidence (traced the SNMP GET handler `mox_snmp_handle_entry` methods 1–4 + daemon side):
- All ies-auto-mibs OIDs register with handler `mox_snmp_handle_entry`; its data sources are ONLY: (1a) `getEntryValue_uriScalar{Config,Status}_*` → `MOXA_SNMP_{CONFIG,STATUS}_URI` → LibFrameworkUri (= **framework** config/status layer); (1b) `getEntryValue_issScalarEntry` → `LibUtil_ExecShCmd(MOXA_SNMP_URI_CTRL_CLIENT --type read --uri…)` (= **ISS** via uri-control-client); (1c) `getEntryValue_generalInfo_*` (MAC/serial/model/portNum) → `LibSystem_*` (in-process shared lib, reads EEPROM/file); (2) `entry_handle_generate_uri_value_file` → framework; (3) `entry_handle_generate_iss_value_file` → ISS. (4) dlmod = **CORRECTION 2026-07-08: earlier "not used" was WRONG — I only checked plugin_moxa_snmp.** There are ~20+ dlmod plugins in OTHER packages, each shipping a `.conf` to `/etc/moxa/netsnmp/config/` that dlmod-loads a `.so` into snmpd, all built on shared `lib_moxa_snmp_plugin` (src/handler/{scalar,table}.c): system_information (config+status), ptp (moxa_1588/moxa_ptp/iec61850/c37_238/ptpbase=5), fiber_check(+event), profinet, dhcp_relay, common_system_event, ui_service_management, iec62439_2, arp_table, dai, config_encryption, utilization, trusted_access, relay, locator, email, … **GOOD NEWS: these dlmod plugins ALL read via `LibFrameworkUri_GetUri` (framework config/status layer) — same backend as ies-auto-mibs, NOT their own daemon/SHM (a few also touch /run/auto_mibs).** So they ARE reachable by the framework broad subagent; convergence = framework subagent serves them in-process + remove the dlmod `.conf`. The "no separate daemon is a subagent" claim stays true; only "method 4 unused" was the error.
- Whole-tree scan of every `getEntryValue_*`: only `LibFrameworkUri_* / LibSystem_* / URI_CTRL_CLIENT` appear — **zero** `socket()/shm_open/shmget/connect()//var/run/…` → no getter talks to a daemon directly.
- `grep agentx|netsnmp_register|SNMPRegisterMib|init_agent` across `app_moxa_*` daemons = empty → **no non-ISS daemon registers OIDs or is a subagent** (only ISS registers, via SNMPRegisterMibWithLock).

Semantics: daemon data physically lives in daemons, but daemons do NOT serve SNMP — they expose data only through the framework config/status layer (Morris layering: daemon → status/config layer → up). So framework is the single window for all non-ISS OIDs; ISS is the only other source.

**SNMPv3 stays at the master (2026-07-13):** USM (auth/priv/engine) + VACM are done entirely by snmpd master; CLI/WEB → plugin_moxa_snmp generates snmpd.conf v3 config. Subagents (ISS, framework) inherit v3 for free — never implement USM/VACM. **Gotcha:** the AgentX PDU the master forwards to a subagent carries OID + context but NOT `securityName` (`agentx_master_handler` in net-snmp master.c). The current in-master ies-auto-mibs reads `reqinfo->asp->pdu->securityName` to map a v3 rwuser → per-user token (`rwuser_list`→`security_tokens`) for config-layer perms; a subagent loses this → per-v3-user config permissions break. Plan D B Task 5 **DECIDED = (a) single internal `snmp` identity**, justified by SRS (`~/WORK/SNMP_50ms/FR-1-8L_SNMP_Software_Requirement_Specification.pdf`): a SNMPv3 user's only permission is binary `authority = read-only|read-write` (`snmp-server user <name> authority {read-only|read-write}`); full-text search found NO fine-grained/per-subtree permission, NO role/privilege mapping, NO audit/change-attribution requirement. That binary RO/RW is already enforced by VACM at the master. So the per-v3-user token machinery (`security_tokens[]`/`rwuser_list[]`/`snmp.<username>` created via `LibUtil_CreateToken`, in both `ies_auto_mibs.c` `utilStoken_update_security_token` and `lib_moxa_snmp_plugin/handler/table.c`) is NOT carried into the subagent — no SRS requirement lost. `security_token` itself = the 3rd arg to `LibFrameworkUri_GetUri/PatchUri` (framework REST auth token, framework does token→`valid_and_get_userinfo`→UserInfo); it's a transport artifact that vanishes in-process (subagent calls `config_operation` directly). The token-file mechanism (`utilStoken_*`) + the two `snmp_script_rust` generators (`generate_iss_snmp_merge_table`/`generate_uri_snmp_table` → `/moxa/run/auto_mibs/*.merge`, consumed by ies-auto-mibs `ies_auto_mibs_handle_iss_remap_merge_table.c`) are all end-of-Plan-D cleanup items, gated on "no snmpd-side LibFrameworkUri caller / nothing reads /moxa/run/auto_mibs/ remains". Also: `MoxaAgentX_SendTrap` dropped — traps are out-of-band (app events → MQTT → trap_notification → /bin/snmptrap); subagent is GET/SET only.

**Plan D sub-project B — Design C LOCKED (2026-07-16, SUPERSEDES Design 2):** the framework subagent **fully owns** each config OID (register RWRITE), and the dlmod is **removed** (stop shipping its config `.conf`). **GET** = in-process `config_operation::get_config_from_path`+`remove_password` (Task 9, done, byte-identical). **SET** = the subagent calls the **same loopback REST PATCH the dlmod does today** (`LibFrameworkUri_PatchUri`/`PostUri` to `/api/v1/setting/data/<uri>?save` with a `LibUtil_CreateToken` admin token) — byte-identical, reuses the whole `setting_write` pipeline incl. `user_mutex`/opmode concurrency coordination, so NO write-path reimplementation and no write risk. **Why C over Design 2 (GET-forward):** SET latency is irrelevant (goal is GET), so accelerating SET has no value; and `rust_moxa_config_layer` is a ported Flask REST service — its ONLY write entry `setting_write` (`lib.rs:467`) is HTTP-shaped (needs `HttpRequest`+`web::Data<AppState>`) with the mutate→check→reload→save orchestration + session/opmode coordination inlined, so there is no request-less `write_config()` a non-HTTP in-process caller could use. C therefore keeps SET on the existing HTTP entry (loopback) and drops the forward trick + shadowed-region/probe + keeping-the-dlmod. **Design C task deltas:** register RWRITE (not RONLY) + add a net-snmp multi-phase SET handler (do the loopback PATCH in MODE_SET_ACTION/COMMIT); remove the dlmod config `.conf` (comment the `dlmod systemInformation` line in `plugin_moxa_system_information/snmp_config/document/snmpd_system_information.conf`) so subagent is sole owner. NO GET-forward, NO probe, NO netsnmp_call_handlers. **stdsnmdb overlap CORRECTION (2026-07-16): `agentx_owned.list` CANNOT skip these** — `net_stdsnmdb.h` sysContact/sysName/sysLocation (`.1.1.4/5/6`) are `HANDLER_CAN_RWRITE`, and `mox_snmp_entry_is_agentx_owned` (`ies_auto_mibs.c:3400`) returns 0 for any `mode & HANDLER_CAN_SET` (RW never skipped, Plan C keeps RW local for ISS). BUT Task 9b verified the subagent's exact-instance `.5.0` (AgentX) WINS dispatch over stdsnmdb's scalar `.5` (in-master) for direct GET+SET even with stdsnmdb present, so the overlap is likely benign. Task 10c = comment the dlmod line + rebuild + verify a full `snmpwalk .1.3.6.1.2.1.1` is byte-identical (no stdsnmdb value/dup at .4/.5/.6); ONLY if the walk shows ambiguity, remove those 3 RW entries from `net_stdsnmdb.h` (rebuilds net-snmp). A scalable "framework-fully-owned skips RW too" mechanism is deferred to B2. **stdsnmdb overlap CONFIRMED BENIGN via pcap (2026-07-16):** with the dlmod removed, `snmpwalk .1.3.6.1.2.1.1` routes GET + GETNEXT (registration ranges `.1.1.4.0→.1.1.4.1` etc.) + SET (TestSet/CommitSet) for `.1.1.1/4/5/6` all to the framework subagent session (sid=8) — the subagent's exact-instance registration fully shadows stdsnmdb's scalar, so NO `net_stdsnmdb.h` edit needed. Task 9b/10c verified: subagent owns config OIDs GET+SET, dlmod `.conf` commented, walk clean & subagent-served. **B1 DONE 2026-07-16:** clean re-test passed (set AAA → get/walk AAA → restore moxa, all consistent; the earlier miss was paste noise); the empty sysDescr/Contact/Location were correct (user had removed the `description "222"` config). Design C proven end-to-end on hardware for `system_information`. Next: B2 (batch-converge more config OID groups the same way).

**URI-path PoC DONE 2026-07-16 (ies-auto-mibs path, not dlmod):** proved the `mox_snmp_handle_entry` (ies-auto-mibs in-master) path can ALSO move to the framework subagent, group-by-group, by **commenting `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY(<group>_MibEntry)` in `ies_auto_mibs_setup.c`** (analogous to removing a dlmod `.conf`; NO skip-list needed since the subagent's exact-instance reg wins + there's no other registrant). PoC target: `net_mx_event_port.h` portOn scalars (`.8691.602.7.1.2.1.1.{1,2.1,2.2}.0`). Key learnings: (1) hand-mapping doesn't scale (net_mx_event_port alone = 60 scalars + 9 tables) → single-source = reuse `net_*.h` (`struct ies_auto_mibs_entry` + `snmp_tools/inc/ies_auto_mibs_handle.h`, `SNMP_DATA_TYPE_INTEGER=0x02`) but couples to product feature-macros — deferred; runtime file (`generate_uri_snmp_table`) is a per-query converter, NOT a mapping dump. (2) **config-boolean ↔ SNMP-INTEGER**: portEvent enable/trap/email are JSON booleans but SNMP INTEGER TruthValues — GET `true→1,false→2` (`get_value.c:95`), SET `1→true,else→false` writing a JSON boolean (`set_value.c:47-56`); handler branches by runtime JSON type (GET) / a fresh read (`config_field_is_bool`, SET). (3) URI = `entry->uri` used directly under `/api/v1/setting/data/` (`IES_URI_CONFIG_PATH`, `get_value.c:71`) → in-process `get_config_from_path(entry->uri)` + PATCH `/api/v1/setting/data/<uri>?save` are byte-identical. (4) SET ~1s (loopback PATCH → check/reload/save pipeline) exceeds snmpset's default 1s timeout → harmless retransmit; SAME latency as the old dlmod (not a regression); GET = ~4ms. New helpers: `ies_config_set_int/_bool`, `MoxaAgentX_SetInt/GetSetInt`, `ASN_INTEGER`. Scalable "framework-fully-owned" mechanism + reuse-header generator still deferred.

**reuse-header (single-source) DONE 2026-07-17:** `lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs/src/mapping_reuse.c` now `#include`s the canonical `net_*.h` (+ `snmp_tools/inc/ies_auto_mibs_handle.h` for the struct + `<net-snmp/agent/net-snmp-agent-includes.h>` for HANDLER_CAN_*), iterates the `ies_auto_mibs_entry` arrays listed in `g_reuse_srcs[]`, and converts scalars (`uri_index=="0"`) to `ies_map_entry` (instance OID = oid_list + .0; skips tables). `lookup.c` merges hand-written seed + reuse. Build: `lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs.mk` copies the product `-D` flag derivation from `3rdparty_net_snmp.mk` (KEEP IN SYNC; MDS_G4000_L3_4XGS/MOXA_DO_RELAY/etc.) + `-I` to the 3rdparty source + `DEPENDENCIES+=3rdparty_net_snmp` (passed via `EXTRA_CFLAGS`). Compiled first try. **GOTCHA: `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY` comment needs `make 3rdparty_net_snmp-dirclean` — plain `-rebuild` skips recompiling `ies_auto_mibs_setup.c` (rsync keeps old mtime).** Proven on HW: after dirclean, mx_event_port tables vanished (ies-auto-mibs no longer registers it) and the ~57 scalars are served by the subagent (single-source works). Adding a group = one line in `g_reuse_srcs[]` + comment its `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY`. **Two follow-ups found:** (1) handler now returns **noSuchInstance** (not genErr) on read failure so a walk survives one bad OID (`MoxaAgentX_SetNoSuchInstance`); walk of `.8691.602.7` now completes (492 lines, End of MIB). (2) **byte-identical needs the runtime URI remap (`mod_uri`)** — e.g. `chainProtectEvent` net_*.h `.uri`=`chainProtectionOn` but the framework config key is `chainProtectOn` (`plugin_moxa_turbo_chain/framework/src/config_event.rs`); ies-auto-mibs uses `mod_uri[0]?mod_uri:uri`, `mod_uri` is empty in static net_*.h and populated at runtime by the merge-table generators — my static reuse misses it, so those OIDs currently return noSuchInstance until the remap is replicated (deferred as "Fix 2"). The old Design-2 content below is superseded.

**Plan D sub-project B — Design 2 LOCKED (2026-07-13, SUPERSEDED by Design C above):** B is a **pure GET-acceleration** project. net-snmp routes an OID's GET+SET to one owner, so instead of the subagent owning the OID, the **existing master-side handler (`mox_snmp_handle_entry` / dlmod GET handler) keeps owning it and serving SET unchanged**, and its **GET branch forwards the read to the framework subagent** (generalize the Plan C ifAdminStatus `netsnmp_call_handlers` trick). Subagent GET is **read-only + identity-less** (VACM authorized at master; per-OID value uniform; fixed `SYS_READ_USERINFO` just to satisfy `get_config_from_path`'s arg; reuse `remove_password_from_config` for byte-identical output). **SET untouched** → `security_token`/per-v3-user machinery stays as-is (so the earlier "(a) single identity" question is moot for B — SET never enters the subagent). **Deferred to later Plan-D phase:** dlmod `.conf` removal / convergence, moving SET in-process. **`lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs` = Layer-1 mapping DATA only** (OID↔URI rows extracted from ies-auto-mibs `net_*.h`, NOT the `.c` handler code — that stays in snmpd). Design 2 drops the docx's Layer-2 (SET dispatch)/Layer-3 (URI actions); URI-from-index assembly lives in the framework Rust GET handler. So sub-project C shrinks to "fill the OID↔URI table", not "extract the 3-layer lib". Design/plan: `~/plan-d-B-framework-agentx-subagent-{design,plan}-2026-07-09.md`. Plan fully rewritten to Design 2 (header + Tasks 6/9/10/11 + B2 + self-review all consistent). **B1 system_information overlap (2026-07-16):** the B1 target `system_information` is a **dlmod plugin** (`plugin_moxa_system_information/snmp_config/snmp_system_information.c` `sSystemInfoOid[]`), reading via `LibFrameworkUri_GetUri(127.0.0.1:80, "/api/v1/setting/data/systemInformation/<field>")` = REST → nginx → actix `_setting_get` (= `config_operation::get_config_from_path` + `remove_password_from_config`, `rust_moxa_config_layer/src/lib.rs:254`). So the subagent GET handler calling those two fns with path = REST-URI-minus-`/api/v1/setting/data/` is **byte-identical** (verified: Task 9 isolation test passed). 6 OIDs, all ASN_OCTET_STR RW: `.8691.602.1.1.1.1.0` sysMoxaDescr, `.8691.602.1.1.1.6.0` sysMoxaDeviceName, `.1.3.6.1.2.1.1.{1,4,5,6}.0` sysDescr/Contact/Name/Location. **Overlap gotcha:** net-snmp builtin mibII is OFF (`--disable-mibs --disable-mib-loading`), but ies-auto-mibs ALSO registers `.1.3.6.1.2.1.1.4/5/6` via `stdsnmdb_MibEntry` (`net_stdsnmdb.h`, URI `stdsnmdb/*` ≠ plugin's `systemInformation/*`), NOT skipped. Today the plugin's exact-instance `.5.0` wins dispatch over ies's scalar `.5`. Clean OIDs (plugin-only, no ies overlap): `.8691.602.x` + sysDescr `.1.1.1`. **Task 10 should forward the clean OIDs first; for the 3 contested std OIDs, add them to `agentx_owned.list` so ies-auto-mibs skips them (Plan C precedent: `ies_auto_mibs_setup.c:290-293` ifmibdb skip → ISS).** `lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs` hand-written rows are an intentional B1 seed; single-source generation from `net_*.h`/plugin defs (and resolving this overlap) is sub-project C, not B.

**B0 DONE 2026-07-16 — framework receives AgentX PDUs as a subagent.** Root-cause of the initial "no connection at all" (pcap: zero SYN/Open-PDU, only ISS sid=6 pinging): the shared **net-snmp was built WITHOUT `agentx/subagent`** — `moxa/package/net/3rdparty_net_snmp/3rdparty_net_snmp.mk:185` `--with-mib-modules` had only `agentx/master`, so libnetsnmpagent lacked `subagent_open_master_session`, and `init_snmp`'s POST_READ_CONFIG→`init_master_agent` was a no-op. **Fix = add `agentx/subagent` to that `--with-mib-modules` list** (now `"ies-auto-mibs/ies_auto_mibs ucd-snmp/dlmod ucd-snmp/proxy agentx/master agentx/subagent"`), then rebuild net-snmp. The `agentx.c` init sequence (set AGENT_ROLE=1 + AGENT_X_SOCKET tcp:127.0.0.1:705 → init_agent → init_snmp → own pthread looping agent_check_and_process(1)) was correct all along. Also note: `<pkg>-rebuild` does NOT recompile Rust binaries (empty Makefile / no BUILD_CMDS) — must run `rust_moxa_build-rebuild` (see [[feedback-build-order]]).

**Both B0 spikes RESOLVED 2026-07-13:** (Task 4) AppState (`rust_moxa_app_state/src/lib.rs`) is all `Arc<std::sync::Mutex<…>>` (not tokio) — subagent clones `Arc::clone(&configs)`+`Arc::clone(&plugins_config)`, `.lock().unwrap()` synchronously, no async bridge; (Task 5) `SYS_READ_USERINFO = user_info::UserInfo { username:"snmp@moxa^service", role: UserInfoRole::admin, nonce:"", from_ip:"127.0.0.1" }` — matches today's SNMP read identity because `LibUtil_CreateToken` (util_shell_cmd.c:201) bakes `-r admin`; `_check_permission` delegates to per-plugin `plugin.check_permission`, so identity must match for byte-identical reads. Next code entry point: plan Task 1 (`lib_moxa_snmp_agentx` C wrapper, pure-new).

**Why:** determines Plan D scope — no need to make each daemon a subagent; ISS + framework cover everything.
**How to apply:** Plan D framework-subagent must retain LibFrameworkUri (config/status layer) + LibSystem + uri-control-client (inherent — it IS the framework). **Design constraint to enforce:** any NEW SNMP OID must read via the config/status layer, never directly from a daemon socket/shm — else the "2 subagents suffice" invariant breaks. Note: the framework/URI path is the ~600ms slow path; Plan D is an architecture/layering win, not a perf win (perf still bounded by the config/status layer). Related: [[project-plan-c-agentx-set-path-and-framing]]. Caveat also noted there: the in-process ifAdminStatus/ifXTable GET-forward (netsnmp_call_handlers to ISS's in-master reg) only works while framework is an in-process dlmod; moving to a subagent breaks it and reopens the RW GET-fast/SET-clean split.
